%N A316868 Number of times 7 appears in decimal expansion of n.
%H A316868 Chris R. Rehmann, <a href="/A316868/b316868.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..9999</a>
%e A316868 a(0) = 0 since the decimal representation of 0 does not contain the digit 7.
%e A316868 a(7) = 1 since 7 appears once in the decimal expansion of 7.
%t A316868 Array[ DigitCount[#, 10, 7] &, 105, 0]
%o A316868 (PARI) a(n) = #select(x->x==7, digits(n)); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Jul 20 2018
%o A316868 (MATLAB)
%o A316868 N = 105; a = arrayfun(@(n) length(strfind(num2str(n),'7')),0:min(N-1,flintmax));
%o A316868 disp(regexprep(num2str(a), ' +', ', ')) % _Chris R. Rehmann_, Oct 11 2026
